        "original_id": "b4a6f8d9-2f88-5013-8ba0-d2548085b803",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Kacha, Sevastopol, Ukraine, Eastern Europe\n- Concepts: territorial status, international recognition, borders\n\nFacts:\n- Ukraine is a sovereign state in Eastern Europe.\n- Ukraine borders Russia to the east and northeast, Belarus to the northwest, Poland, Hungary, and Slovakia to the west, Romania and Moldova to the southwest, and the Black Sea and Sea of Azov to the south and southeast.\n- Kacha is an urban-type settlement under the City of Sevastopol's jurisdiction.\n- The territory including Kacha is recognized by a majority of countries as part of Ukraine and is incorporated by Russia as part of the Crimean Federal District.",
